<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="TanMenu.Wpf.Views.Settings.ToolsCard">
  <!-- One settings row — icon, title + secondary line, master ToggleSwitch — with a bordered, scrolling
       list of per-tool CheckBoxes on its expansion row, inside the same tm-card Border. See the "row
       spec's shared classes" block in Themes/Fluent2/Launcher.axaml for the anatomy, and
       AppearanceCard's code-behind for the full ReloadFromConfig contract every settings card group
       follows.

       Round 5, item 3: the list used to hang below the row's Grid inside a wrapping StackPanel, indented
       by a hand-written Margin="30,10,0,0". It is now the Grid's own second row spanning columns 1-2, so
       its left edge comes from column 1 rather than from a constant that happened to equal the icon
       column's width plus its margin, and its right edge reaches the card's content edge instead of
       stopping wherever the widest tool name did.

       The CheckBoxes inside the bordered list sit a little further in — the list Border's own Padding
       and 1 px stroke, plus each CheckBox's own template padding. That padding was 8,4 and measured
       9.33 DIP of total inset; Round 7, Task 7 re-derived it to 7,5 on vis-layout's published ladder
       ("between related controls — 4 / 7", and 5 relative pixels as the minimum separation), which
       moves the inset by 1 DIP and is not re-measured here. Either way it is the list control's
       business, not the row spec's: the spec constrains where a row's expansion CONTENT starts, which
       is this Border's left edge.

       Round 7, Task 3 gave the CheckBox an Aero template, and this list is where that lands hardest.
       Measured with UI Automation on the live page at 150 %, on the eight tools config.json ships with,
       on a build with the change and a build without:

         each CheckBox   237-339 x 48 physical  ->  1750 x 29   (Auto width -> stretched; 32 -> 19.33 DIP tall)
         row pitch       56 physical            ->  37          (the 3,3 code-set Margin is unchanged)
         list content    8 x 56 = 448 physical  ->  8 x 37 = 296  (299 DIP -> 197 DIP)
         element left    x = 3035 physical      ->  x = 3035    (UNCHANGED)

       The left edge did not move, so the 9.33 DIP above still describes where a row starts; what the
       Aero template drops is the leading inset INSIDE the control. A PrintWindow row scan across the
       first checkbox puts the 13 DIP box's first ink column at exactly x = 3035, the element's own left
       edge, where Fluent's template held it further in.

       MaxHeight="240" on the ScrollViewer (ported verbatim from SettingsWindow's 常用工具 tab) is what
       keeps a long DefaultTools list (config.json is user-editable — see the code-behind) from pushing
       whatever settings groups come after this one off screen. It still does, but it no longer BINDS on
       the shipped list: at 299 DIP of content the eight default tools used to overflow 240 and this
       ScrollViewer showed a vertical bar (measured 24 x 360 physical); at 197 DIP they fit, the bar is
       gone, and the clamp now starts biting at roughly twelve tools instead of roughly seven. -->
  <StackPanel>
    <TextBlock x:Name="GroupHead" Classes="tm-group-head" />

    <Border Classes="tm-card">
      <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto">
        <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="tm-icon tm-card-icon" Text="&#xE90F;" />
        <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Classes="tm-card-text">
          <TextBlock x:Name="ShowToolsTitle" Classes="tm-card-title" />
          <TextBlock x:Name="ShowToolsSub" Classes="tm-card-sub" />
        </StackPanel>
        <ToggleSwitch Grid.Column="2" x:Name="ShowToolsToggle" Classes="tm-card-toggle"
                      IsCheckedChanged="OnShowToolsChanged" />

        <!-- Disabled (not hidden) while ShowToolsToggle is off — ported verbatim from
             SettingsWindow.BuildToolCheckboxes ("Unchecking only disables the list; the individual
             states stay and are still persisted"): the per-tool Show values keep whatever the user set
             so re-enabling the category does not silently reset which tools it contains. -->
        <Border Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Classes="tm-card-expander"
                Padding="7,5"
                BorderBrush="{DynamicResource StrokeControlBrush}" BorderThickness="1"
                CornerRadius="{DynamicResource RadiusControl}">
          <ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" MaxHeight="240">
            <StackPanel x:Name="ToolsPanel" />
          </ScrollViewer>
        </Border>
      </Grid>
    </Border>
  </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
